    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (78.15) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19) headline the roster as our primary offensive engines. **Bryce Harper** occupies the top spot in our rankings, buoyed by an elite 0.400 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Brady Singer. His upside is amplified by his projected lead-off role, ensuring maximum plate appearances. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a significant platoon edge against D. Peterson, making him a high-efficiency start despite the moderate skill of the opposing arm. We are also leaning heavily into the Colorado wind, which significantly lifts the daily scores for **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (66.57) against Ryan Feltner; their ability to put the ball in play combined with favorable weather patterns makes them core components of our 5x5 strategy today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **JJ Bleday** (51.32). While **JJ Bleday** shows strong potential, his score was suppressed by a difficult matchup against Jes\u00fas Luzardo, whose elite strikeout profile significantly lowers the run-scoring expectation. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor provided by the daily efficiency of **Jonathan Aranda** (56.90) and the specific platoon advantages exploited by **Gavin Sheets** (63.23) against a vulnerable Merrill Kelly. We remain cautious regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Luis Arraez**, **Zack Gelof**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**; should any of these players be held out of their respective lineups, we must ensure our game-cap management remains disciplined. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined on the IL, our depth\u2014including **Masyn Winn** and **Dylan Beavers**\u2014stands ready should we need to pivot to preserve our remaining games for the week.",
